+\subsection{SAM3 Adaptation on GeoFWI3D}
+\label{sec:sam3-methods}
+
+The geological adaptation study starts from the general SAM~3 checkpoint
+\cite{carion2025sam3}, with fresh LoRA factors whose initial output is
+zero. Only the 18,497,664 adapter parameters are optimized; the base
+weights remain frozen. This initialization contains no medical adapter.
+The fixed query is \emph{salt body}, and the output classes are salt and
+background. Whole-volume predictions are reconstructed from image slices
+and this query, without reference-mask localization prompts.
+
+The design crosses folds 0, 1 and 3 with seeds 0, 1 and 2 and fourteen
+objectives, giving 126 planned runs. Each fold uses five labelled support
+volumes, selected as the first five of its established geological support
+list, and 96 held-out volumes. Supports remain fixed across seeds and
+objectives. Every run receives 25 optimizer updates without augmentation,
+using two adjacent-slice pairs per update. The learning-rate schedule
+retains its 200-update horizon, 20-update warmup and rates of
+$5\times10^{-5}$ and $5\times10^{-6}$; training uses its first 25 updates.
+This is a fixed adaptation schedule, separate from the geological
+FLOP-capped comparison.
+
+The baseline retains SAM3's native detection, presence and mask losses;
+\texttt{dice} in the run identifiers is a naming convention, not a
+Dice-only objective. Auxiliary coefficients target a median gradient
+ratio of 0.1 with a 95th-percentile cap of 0.5. Bands are calibrated at
+initialization for each fold/seed cell; the other selected terms are
+calibrated after five prefix updates, using four sampled pairs per
+support volume. Coefficients then remain fixed. Spatial targets use
+source-array voxel geometry. Evaluation uses the final adapter and
+records per-volume salt Dice and foreground FN/FP on both support and
+held-out volumes. The completion inventory is reported separately in
+Section~\ref{sec:sam3-results}.
+
